ssible tiles to discard.\n\nFirst, let's consider the tiles I have and how they can form melds. My current hand has:\n\n- W1, W2, W7 (from the meld? No, the meld is already formed. Wait, my meld is [W6, W7, W8], so the W7 in the meld is from the previous player's discard. My hand has W1, W2, and another W7. So that W7 is in my hand. So if I discard that W7, someone else could use it for a meld. But if I keep it, maybe I can use it for another meld.\n\nLooking at my hand, I need to form four melds and a pair. I already have one meld (W6-7-8). So I need three more melds and a pair. Let's see:\n\nPossible melds:\n\n- W1 and W2: If I can get a W3, I can form a Chow of W1-2-3. But I don't have a W3. The unshown count for W3 is 4, so possible.\n\n- T1: If I can get T2 and T3, a Chow of T1-2-3. But I don't have those. Unshown T2 is 4, T3 is 3.\n\n- T6, T7 (two), T8: That's a Chow of T6-7-8. So if I have T6, T7, T8, that's a Chow. I have T6 and T8, and two T7s. So I can form a T6-7-8 Chow with one T7. The remaining T7 could be part of another Chow if I have T5 or T9. But I don't have those.\n\n- B1 and B5 (two): If I can get another B5, a Pung. Or maybe a Chow if I have B4 and B6. But B4 is 3 left, B6 is 3. So if I get B4 and B6, I can form a B4-5-6 Chow. But I have B5 (two). So if I have B4 and B6, that's possible. But I don't have them now.\n\n- Pairs: I have T7 (two), B5 (two). So possible pairs. If I can form pairs, that helps.\n\nSo, considering that, maybe the best approach is to aim for forming two Chows (W1-2-3 and T6-7-8) and a Pung of B5, plus a pair. But I need to see if that's feasible.\n\nAlternatively, maybe forming a Pung of B5 if I can get another one. Since I have two B5s, getting another would make a Pung. There are four B5s left, so possible.\n\nBut which tile to discard now? Let's look at the valid actions again: Play W7, T6, W2, B1, T7, T1, B5, W1, T8.\n\nIf I discard W7, that's a middle tile. If I discard T6, that's a terminal. Discarding W2 or W1 woul